  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{3}{35}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{35}{x}^{3}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[(-1)^{3}-(-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}(-1+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
